<!-- ===== SECTION 2: CREATING ARRAYS ===== -->
<section class="section reveal" id="creating-arrays">
  <span class="section-label">Core Concepts</span>
  <h2>Creating NumPy Arrays</h2>

  <p>NumPy provides multiple ways to create arrays: from Python lists, special functions for common patterns (zeros, ones), and generation functions (arange, linspace). Each method serves specific use cases in data science workflows.</p>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="kw">import</span> <span class="nm">numpy</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="nm">np</span>

<span class="cm"># From Python list</span>
<span class="va">arr1</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">np</span>.<span class="fn">array</span>([<span class="nm">1</span>, <span class="nm">2</span>, <span class="nm">3</span>])

<span class="cm"># Special arrays</span>
<span class="va">zeros</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">np</span>.<span class="fn">zeros</span>((<span class="nm">3</span>, <span class="nm">4</span>))  <span class="cm"># 3x4 matrix of zeros</span>
<span class="va">ones</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">np</span>.<span class="fn">ones</span>(<span class="nm">5</span>)             <span class="cm"># 1D array of ones</span>
<span class="va">identity</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">np</span>.<span class="fn">eye</span>(<span class="nm">3</span>)         <span class="cm"># 3x3 identity matrix</span>

<span class="cm"># Ranges</span>
<span class="va">arange</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">np</span>.<span class="fn">arange</span>(<span class="nm">0</span>, <span class="nm">10</span>, <span class="nm">2</span>)  <span class="cm"># [0,2,4,6,8]</span>
<span class="va">linspace</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">np</span>.<span class="fn">linspace</span>(<span class="nm">0</span>, <span class="nm">1</span>, <span class="nm">5</span>) <span class="cm"># 5 evenly spaced points</span></code></pre>
  <div class="code-explain">
    <p><strong>What is happening here:</strong> np.array() converts lists to arrays. zeros/ones create arrays filled with those values—useful for placeholders in algorithms. arange is like Python's range but returns arrays. linspace is crucial for creating evaluation grids, especially in visualization.</p>
  </div>

